    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Who is the best water heater company in Richardson, TX?</h3><p>For 2026, our top pick is Koen Plumbing, Inc., headquartered on N. Bowser Road in Richardson and operating since 1946. Dean's Plumbing, also Richardson-based, is a strong second option, publishing both tank and tankless replacement with same-day service.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Does a water heater replacement in Richardson need a permit?</h3><p>Yes, in most cases. Texas plumbing code generally requires a permit and inspection for water heater replacement, including a drain pan and expansion tank where applicable. A licensed plumber typically pulls the permit as part of the job.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Is tankless worth it for an older Richardson home?</h3><p>It depends on the home. Many older Richardson houses have a compact garage or closet water heater setup, and a tankless conversion can free up that space, but it often requires larger gas line sizing and new venting, which adds to the upfront cost compared to a like-for-like tank swap.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>How much does water heater replacement cost in Richardson?</h3><p>A standard 40-50 gallon tank replacement typically runs $1,200-$2,500 installed in North Texas, while tankless conversions run higher, often $3,000-$6,000, depending on gas line and venting work required.</p></div>
